OM events (feed() does not touch mouse.t).\",\n    \"The whole fighting rule set: a karate Bout with the referee's phase machine, half and full points, counters, aiuchi, the clock and hantei; the twin-stick control reader; the CPU with reaction delay and personalities; the three bonus games; the gibberish voice synth; the glyph icons; 10-foot menus and the attract director.\",\n    \"Knowing which engine pieces to avoid. E.Fighter and E.Match assume life bars, game.freeze stalls update (which would stall networking), and the 5x7 font has no cross, circle, square or triangle, so none of the stock fighting helpers fit. Also hand-balancing the AI so levels and personalities ordered sensibly.\",\n    \"Two small edits, listed in engine/CHANGES.md: the button symbols default to PlayStation (setting and Input.glyphs) because TASK.md asks for it, and game.live keeps the scene update running while the pause menu is open so a shared-world host never stalls its network traffic. Everything else (right stick as the technique stick through input.padAim, glyph icons, voices) was done game-side.\",\n    \"A 'next step' hook-free way to change scenes: let game.go take effect at once in headless runs (or expose a flush), and make scene objects instances instead of shared singletons so state left on the object cannot leak into the next visit.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The plan was a complete, ordered build document: exact technique tables, scoring formulas, phase timings, message formats and a traceability table. Having the numbers decided made the combat code straightforward, and the hub protocol section meant the harness passed at the first run.\",\n    \"The plan and TASK.md disagree on small things (file names in the plan carry the planner's model and time, the plan asks for edits like EC1 and EC7 that the engine did not need), and the plan's scale (all 11 locations, a Technique Lab, a 2.5D camera, the bull as a custom creature, 4 online roles, all tests) is bigger than one medium-effort pass, so every item needed a decision on how much to cut.\",\n    \"Making the CPU and the balance work: the plan's targets (a level curve, win rates, every technique landing, no technique over 35 percent) conflict with a roster where a single lunge or jump kick scores a full point from long range, so the data and the AI both needed tuning passes.\",\n    \"Say which parts of a long plan are mandatory and which are stretch, tell the builder that a plan's tables may be tuned for balance when a test says so, and give a total size budget. A line on the expected size of the final single file would also help.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Karate Champon\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Two sticks. One clean strike.\",\n    \"description\": \"A point-sparring karate tournament inspired by Karate Champ: land one clean technique and let the referee call it. Climb from white belt to Champ, break boards, smash flying pots and stop a charging bull, then play winner-stays-on Kachinuki with friends.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Fighting\",\n    \"source\": \"Karate Champ (1984)\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Left stick/WASD: move, jump, crouch · Right stick, face buttons or IJKL: techniques · Options/Esc: pause\",\n    \"tags\": [\"2d\", \"arcade\", \"versus\", \"retro\", \"pixel art\", \"comedy\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\nnode tests/run.mjs --only ui 2>&1 | head -12","timeout":400000}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01LVjA1X151TeDarQsJNmPNV":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184016__x1295cd/work/KarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-184016"}}}
