{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh8Xopy9AFHPUzMhNRhb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've now built two of the three plan features the hook flagged: the Technique Lab and Mei in the front crowd. I did not build the 2.5D \"Tatami\" camera. After a full run and then a re-run of the lab and smoke suites with a fix, the tests passed (777 in the full run, with one lab failure that was fixed and re-run). I did not repeat the full command after the last fix.\n\n- **Technique Lab:** it's a new scene, reachable from the Dojo menu, the dev WARP tab, or `#lab/<technique>` in the URL.\n  - It shows the hero against a standing dummy and cycles all 15 scoring techniques.\n  - It shows frame data, the table reach, and a contact gap measured by sweeping distances in the real rules. Tests check that the measured gap matches the table within 4 units.\n  - Replay, slow motion and a box overlay are included.\n  - The plan's live per-technique sliders and \"copy JSON\" button are not built; the global dev sliders still work.\n- **Mei in the crowd:** she cheers from the front row of every stage after the harbor: bamboo, log bridge, ship, market, Fuji garden and the stadium. A test checks the stadium.\n- **2.5D camera:** not built. TASK.md only asks me to pick a fitting camera, and the side view is that pick. A tilted view would break the hand-painted stage floors and backdrops, so adding it would mean redrawing every stage.\n\nThe Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections in my previous reply still apply. The bundled `.html` and `exit-interview.json` are in the task folder root, rebuilt with these changes, and the exit interview still parses."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":482,"cache_read_input_tokens":584771,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemera